# Every text file checks out with LF line endings on every platform, Windows included, where
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise turn them CRLF. Without this, a test that reads the
# package's own source (a script's block, the autoload manifest, a golden fixture) passes on
# macOS and Linux and fails on Windows, and Prettier reads every web/src file as unformatted.
# text=auto keeps binary files (images, the mp3s, PDFs) binary. A checkout that predates this
# line keeps its CRLF files until they are checked out again.
* text=auto eol=lf
